// Analyzed file list for tasks/corundum_tx_rx_datapath.
//
// Read by two consumers, which is why one list holds every source:
//   * lists/tc_elab.tcl:  analyze -sv12 -f lists/tc_elab.files
//   * taskdefs.slang_args, which filters it into tc_elab.files.slang for the
//     local Slang gate and the design map.
//
// v5/round.py appends one `../submission/<worker>.sv` line per worker at the
// end, so ORDER MATTERS and the file must end with a newline: the upstream RTL
// comes first, then the formal top that instantiates it, then the candidate
// targets that bind into the formal top, and a worker's file must come last so
// it can reference anything above it.
//
// Paths are relative to the package root -- the drivers `cd $task_root` before
// sourcing tc_elab.tcl, and `slang` is run from there too.
//
// No `+incdir+` and no `+define+`. Corundum's RTL is self-contained Verilog
// 2001: not one of the 28 files below has an `include or reads a macro that is
// not defined in the same file.
//
// WHERE EACH FILE CAME FROM. The clone carries more than one copy of some
// library modules and only one may be analyzed or the module is declared
// twice:
//   * `priority_encoder.v` from fpga/lib/pcie/rtl/ (identical to the axis copy);
//   * `arbiter.v` and `axis_arb_mux.v` from fpga/lib/axis/rtl/, which is the
//     copy `rx_fifo` and the two op muxes were written against. The pcie copy
//     of `arbiter.v` differs only in whether the register update sits in the
//     reset `else` branch; the axis copy of `axis_arb_mux.v` is the one with
//     `UPDATE_TID`, which `rx_fifo` sets.
// `fpga/lib/axis` is a symlink to `fpga/lib/eth/lib/axis`, so those two paths
// name the same file.

// ---- upstream Corundum RTL, byte-identical ------------------------------
//      github.com/corundum/corundum @ 1ca0151b (2023-12-02)

//      fpga/lib/axis/rtl/ -- the AXI-Stream library the frame buffers use
rtl/corundum/priority_encoder.v
rtl/corundum/arbiter.v
rtl/corundum/axis_fifo.v
rtl/corundum/axis_adapter.v
rtl/corundum/axis_fifo_adapter.v
rtl/corundum/axis_demux.v
rtl/corundum/axis_arb_mux.v

//      fpga/lib/pcie/rtl/ -- the DMA client library
rtl/corundum/dma_psdpram.v
rtl/corundum/dma_client_axis_source.v
rtl/corundum/dma_client_axis_sink.v

//      fpga/common/rtl/ -- the descriptor / completion machinery
rtl/corundum/queue_manager.v
rtl/corundum/cpl_queue_manager.v
rtl/corundum/desc_op_mux.v
rtl/corundum/desc_fetch.v
rtl/corundum/cpl_op_mux.v
rtl/corundum/cpl_write.v

//      fpga/common/rtl/ -- the transmit datapath
rtl/corundum/tx_checksum.v
rtl/corundum/mqnic_egress.v
rtl/corundum/tx_engine.v
rtl/corundum/mqnic_interface_tx.v
rtl/corundum/tx_fifo.v

//      fpga/common/rtl/ -- the receive datapath
rtl/corundum/rx_checksum.v
rtl/corundum/rx_hash.v
rtl/corundum/mqnic_ingress.v
rtl/corundum/mqnic_rx_queue_map.v
rtl/corundum/rx_engine.v
rtl/corundum/mqnic_interface_rx.v
rtl/corundum/rx_fifo.v

// ---- task-authored formal top: the chain, the three ring drivers, the four
//      bounded host-memory responders and the two MAC links ---------------
ft/corundum_tx_rx_datapath_ft.sv

// ---- task-authored oracle, candidate targets and covers -----------------
sva/targets_corundum_tx_rx_datapath.sv
